------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Provenance
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The encoder and decoder are original implementations written from the prose
and tables of RFC 6716 (Definition of the Opus Audio Codec) as updated by
RFC 8251, and from RFC 7845 (Ogg Encapsulation for Opus) for the
identification header and channel mappings. libopus, FFmpeg and other
implementations were not read, copied or translated. Where RFC 6716 makes
the reference code attached to it (Appendix A) normative, it was used as
specification only: the CELT layer's normative behaviour was described in
prose by one author (docs/CELT_SPEC.md) and implemented from that
description by another who did not read the code, and the opus_compare
conformance metric used by the tests was re-implemented from a description.
Constant tables were extracted from the RFC text by scripts or derived from
their definitions (see docs/PROVENANCE.md). The SILK output resampler is an
original least-squares design; no filter or table was fitted to any
decoder's output.

The official Opus test vectors (opus_testvectors-rfc8251, published by the
Opus project and the IETF) are used as data only, downloaded at test time;
they are not part of this package.

